## Technical Requirements

Make sure to read annotations in Figma!

### organism/MegaMenuMobile/MegaMenuMobile.vue

```
interface MegaMenuMobileProps {
  isOpen: boolean;
  isUserLoggedIn: boolean;
}
```

### Notes : 

* this is the wrapper component, rendering the default sheet and the "Login" button.
* It's responsible for rendering either the RootMenu or ChildMenu depending on the navigation state
* use LuiButton , RootMenu , ChildMenu , Luisheet 

### organism/MegaMenuMobile/RootMenu.vue

![](blob:https://media.staging.atl-paas.net/?type=file&localId=null&id=d2f3da06-ffbe-452c-8998-17b3f9527730&&collection=&height=749&occurrenceKey=null&width=347&__contextId=null&__displayType=null&__external=false&__fileMimeType=null&__fileName=null&__fileSize=null&__mediaTraceId=null&url=null)
```
interface MobileMenuItem extends CategoryNodeCompactProps {
  id: string;
  subItems : mobileMenuItem[];
}

interface RootMenuProps {
  colorMode : 'on-light' | 'on-dark';
  headline : string;
  href? : string;
  contentHeadline? : string;
  navigationLinks? : mobileMenuListProps;
  items : MobileMenuItem[];
}
```

### **Notes:**

* do not implement the header this is for content only
* add content slot below category nodes
* check Caro's guidelines on figma
* use `LuiText` , `LuiIcon` , `LuiMobileMenuitem` , `LuiInpageNavigationCompactGrid` , `LuiLanguageSwitcher` , `LuiDarkModeSwitch`, `LuiMobileMenuList`

### organism/MegaMenuMobile/ChildMenu.vue

![](blob:https://media.staging.atl-paas.net/?type=file&localId=null&id=edfd73ea-dea3-489d-b9a2-e386c054599b&&collection=&height=873&occurrenceKey=null&width=343&__contextId=null&__displayType=null&__external=false&__fileMimeType=null&__fileName=null&__fileSize=null&__mediaTraceId=null&url=null)
* Add content slot for below the category nodes

### Storybook stories

Add a storybook-story similar [to this one](https://storybook.laioutr.cloud/?path=/story/molecules-sheet--default&globals=viewport:s). Clicking a button opens the mobile menu. Clicking a category-node in the RootMenu changes the content to ChildMenu.
